<Base title="Disclosure" description="How NeonKey handles affiliate links, sponsorships and free products, and why they never decide a verdict.">
  <article class="narrow page-head prose">
    <span class="kicker">Disclosure</span>
    <h1>Affiliate &amp; sponsorship disclosure</h1>
    <div class="callout warn">Placeholder text for the demo. Have it reviewed before launch.</div>
    <p>Some links on NeonKey are affiliate links. If you buy through one, NeonKey may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Affiliate relationships never decide a verdict or ranking.</li>
      <li>Pages with affiliate links show a disclosure at the top.</li>
      <li>Sponsored content, if any, will be clearly labeled "Sponsored."</li>
      <li>Products sent for free will be disclosed in the review.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This follows the spirit of the FTC's Endorsement Guides. See the FTC's guidance at <a data-umami-event="outbound-click" data-umami-event-item="ftc-endorsement-guides" href="https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/ftcs-endorsement-guides-what-people-are-asking">ftc.gov</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
